<title>USA: UAW, GM  reach tentative agreement to end strike.</title>
<headline>UAW, GM  reach tentative agreement to end strike.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Auto Workers union said they reached a tentative agreement with General Motors Corp. Friday night to end a parts plant strike that had forced GM to idle six assembly plants in the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>UAW Local 909 Financial Secretary Jim Marcum said details of the agreement would not be released until a ratification vote set for Sunday morning. The strike by 2,800 workers at the Warren, Mich., powertrain plant began at midnight Tuesday when a new agreement could be not be reached by the strike deadline.</p>
</text>
